    "breadcrumb": "Podpora Swing Catalyst \u003e Softvér a Funkcie",
    "content": "Ako exportovať dáta na prezeranie v tabuľkovom procesore Tento článok sa zaoberá exportom surových dát zo Swing Catalyst alebo Motion Catalyst ako tsv súbory.\nPoznámka: súbory exportované okrem podrobností o študentoch sú oddelené tabulátormi. Uistite sa, že ste si vybrali oddelenie tabulátorom v prehliadači tabuľkového procesora.\nLooking to export student information? See this article.\nThere are several ways to export data, through the Explorer and from the stack. Both options allow the same functionality.\nExporting data from the Explorer In the Explorer data can be exported by right clicking on a recording, selecting Export and choosing from the available options, or dragging the recording(s) to the Export List.\nMenu selection\nFunction\nAdd recording to export list Adds the selected recording to the export list. Same as dragging the recording to the export list\nAdd session to export list Adds a whole session to the export list. Amount of recordings that appear in the export list\ndepend on how many recordings are in the session itself.\nExport recording as raw data files Exports the selected recording with the raw data export options\nExport session as raw data files Exports the whole session with raw data export options\nAn overview of the export options that are available by right clicking:\nThe export list:\nData Export selection It’s possible to choose from a few different options when exporting data.\nThis article mainly focuses on raw data.\nTo export raw data, make sure to select “Raw Data” in the Export dialog.\nRaw Data options Please note that this functionality is still being improved on, currently a lot of options are bundled with “Raw data”.\nLast updated: 2023-12-15 | View on official support site",
